# HEC receiver token map — template.
#
# Copy to .secrets next to hec_receiver.py (or, preferably, provide via a
# systemd credential — see hec_receiver.service). Then:
#
#   chmod 640 .secrets && chown root:wazuh .secrets
#
# Format: comma-separated <token>:<source>:<namespace> triplets.
#   token      — long random secret, one per sender: openssl rand -hex 32
#   source     — becomes the top-level "integration" field for that sender
#   namespace  — short prefix (2-4 chars) wrapping the sender's payload,
#                same convention as wodle integrations (op, pp, xdr, ...)
#
# Per-source tokens enable per-source revocation: remove a triplet and
# restart the receiver to cut off one sender without touching the others.
#
# If your edge has no pre-origin auth (e.g. Tailscale Funnel), the token is
# the ONLY auth layer — long random tokens and scheduled rotation are
# mandatory, not recommended. See docs/guides/security-checklist.md.

HEC_TOKENS=REPLACE_WITH_RANDOM_HEX_TOKEN_1:examplevendor:exv,REPLACE_WITH_RANDOM_HEX_TOKEN_2:othersource:osr
